OL,3,GNEWSAKeeping prison closed 'crazy' says
OL,4,ATory deputy
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe decision to keep a prison closed
OL,7,Fdue to concerns over the levels of a
OL,8,Fnaturally occurring, radioactive gas at
OL,9,Fthe site, has been described as "crazy"
OL,10,Fby the deputy leader of the
OL,11,FConservatives.
OL,13,FAlex Burghart said reopening Dartmoor
OL,14,FPrison would free up hundreds of cells
OL,15,F- it closed in 2024 after elevated
OL,16,Flevels of radon gas were discovered.
OL,18,FHe believed the 600 capacity jail could
OL,19,Fhelp ease overcrowding, and reduce the
OL,20,Fneed to release prisoners early to free
OL,21,Fup space.
OL,23,APub: 02-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
